{"id":"e2e-scratch-sharing","parent":"perfc-tests","ord":"a0","title":"63% of e2e scenarios spawn a private server — share one scratch corpus per feature where files are disjoint","done":"2026-08-20T11:12:01-04:00","desc":"555 of 875 scenarios are @scratch: — each a corpus copy plus an olai process spawned and killed. Families like the_agent (82) and html_previews (32) write disjoint files and could share one scratch corpus per FEATURE instead of per scenario.\n- Worth more wall time than all 150 audit cuts combined; also where the flake census (underload.sh) says the port/lock failures come from.\n- Deliberately out of the e2e-earn-browser cut lane's scope — an infra change with its own risk profile.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #281 (Grok, merged 232c1f8b7), with the premise revised by its own census.** The mechanism: `@share-scratch` on a feature → one corpus copy + one server per feature PER WORKER; collisions OBSERVED by content-hashing the scratch tree after each scenario and failing loudly naming both scenarios and the file; `@own-scratch` opts a scenario out (refused without the feature tag); a shared scenario that restarts its server is refused (`restartGate`, pinned). Census after the cut: 59 features, 724 scenarios, 490 `@scratch`.\n- **What did not hold:** the_agent (76) is NOT file-disjoint — the agent writes the same outlines and conversation state lives in the server and XDG; the UI-edit families all mutate one outline; it_stays_live/backlinks read the original corpus that later scenarios mutate (a write-only observer cannot catch that). Converted: html_previews (19 share / 9 own) and documents (2 / 1) — 16 of 502 spawns saved; converted-file underload 3 runs / 0 drops.\n- What is left is filed: `e2e-scratch-restore-between` (restore files under a live server so overlapping writers could share) and `e2e-underload-full-census` (the full-scale flake census).","created":"2026-08-19T20:50:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"the e2e audit 2026-08-19"}}
{"id":"e2e-scratch-restore-between","parent":"perfc-tests","ord":"a1","title":"e2e: restore files between scenarios #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T18:40:24-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node first; opencode classified this one as real work left, not a finding).\n- #281 shares one scratch + one server per feature per worker only where scenarios' writes are DISJOINT, observed by content hash; a feature whose scenarios rewrite the same file keeps per-scenario copies.\n- Restoring the corpus between scenarios under the still-running server would let overlapping writers share as well — but the store is entitled not to notice a same-length rewrite (the evidence README already says so), so a restore needs a signal the server honours, not just bytes put back. That is the design question.\n- Payoff ceiling: the UI-edit families (keyboard_editing, undo, dragdrop_multiselect, palette_actions, split_and_merge, trash, edge_editing — ~150 scenarios) are the ones this would reach; chat features stay private regardless (server/XDG conversation state).","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral"}}
