{"id":"transcript-stream-quadratic","parent":"perfc-server","ord":"a3","title":"Streaming a chat answer ships the whole row per token — 323× the answer's bytes over the wire","doing":true,"desc":"**Symptom:** chat answers stream in slow, lumpy pulses from a kolu-bot server (India) to a laptop (Canada) over a DIRECT tailnet (~250ms RTT, DERP ruled out).\\n\\n**Measured on kolu-bot** (opencode ACP, a 5-paragraph answer): 3,218 answer bytes arrived as **643 message chunks averaging 5 bytes each**.\\n\\n**The wire cost:** the chat publishes `transcript.say(text)` on every chunk (chat.ts:435), which UPSERTS the whole growing row into the `transcript` deltas collection — the full text-so-far, not the new chunk. So the bytes crossing the socket are the sum of prefixes, O(N²): **1,039,111 bytes for a 3,218-byte answer — 323× amplification.** And the deltas coalescer flushes per microtask (kolu server.ts:2742), and each agent chunk is its own stdin event, so it is ~one websocket frame per chunk: **~640 frames**, each heavier than the last. On a high-RTT link, hundreds of small-then-large TCP writes pace badly (ACK-clocked), which is the lumpy feel; on a LAN the whole thing is invisible.\\n\\n**Fix:**\\n- Stream APPENDS, not rows: a chunk rides as a delta carrying only its new text (seq-keyed on the row), so the wire carries ~O(N) — the answer's own size, once.\\n- Time-coalesce the transcript flush (~100–200ms) so a turn is a few dozen frames, not ~640. Collections have no `coalesceMs` today (only local-authority cells do, kolu define.ts:182) — the time-based half is a small kolu ask; the append shape is olai's.\\n- The browser appends text to the row and throttles the Markdown re-render to the same cadence.\\n\\n**Not this node (separate):** the model itself was slow here — first token at 7.3s, 14.6s stream span for 3.2KB (kimi-k3 via LiteLLM from India). That is provider latency, not the wire; a Claude chat on the same server would isolate it.","created":"2026-08-22T08:39:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T08:45:25-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-22 (slow streaming, Canada↔India direct tailnet); measured on kolu-bot"}}
